</TextLines>
</Shape>
<Shape Id="32" Type="Text" Sheet="0" Angle="0" HorzAlign="Left" VertAlign="Top" TextAlign="Left" FontVector="Y" FontSize="90" FontWidth="-2" FontScale="1" FontColor="12632256" LineSpacing="1.2">
<Points>
<Point X="-27.139291" Y="-11.295227"/>
</Points>
<FontName>Tahoma</FontName>
<TextLines>
<TextLine>Reviewed PCB832 revX3_5.dchxml. Items 2 and 5 still have missing connections.</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>1 — Corrected. R23 = 95.3 kΩ and R18 = 1 MΩ, with the correct connections for internal VSET, 3.3 V, 1 MHz, automatic PFM/PWM and discharge disabled.</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>2 — Input corrected; output still incomplete. 12vdc_digital now feeds U4 VIN/EN and C14. But L2 pin 1 and U4 pin 3/VOS connect only to each other—no output capacitor or system-supply connection.</TextLine>
<TextLine>Add the 22 µF output capacitor between that common node and GND_digital.</TextLine>
<TextLine>The connection onward to 3v3_digital still needs completing, with reverse-current handling resolved before directly joining the two converter outputs.</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>3 — Requested wiring is now correct. R24 pulls up from 12vdc_digital; TPS62902RPJR_PG connects directly to Q7’s gate; R25 is gate-to-ground. Both resistors are 100 kΩ. Tentative remains appropriate: this verifies wiring, not power-transfer behavior.</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>4 — Corrected. The internal ties resolve to physical pads 3↔4 and 6↔7, on VOUT and SW respectively.</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>5 — Driver added, but GPIO connection missing. Connect U1 pin 22 / GPIO14 to DURA_LCD_BL, which currently contains only R31 pin 2. Leave R31 pin 1 connected to Q9’s gate.</TextLine>
<TextLine>This stage is active-high/default-OFF, unlike the earlier fail-ON plan. Current firmware is still configured active-low.</TextLine>
<TextLine>Backlight current limiting and the transistor’s suitability at the resulting approximately 3 V gate drive remain unverified.</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>6 — Understood; no schematic DNP marking required. C11 remains correctly connected VG-to-ground, 1 µF. C10 population is controlled in Layout, as you explained.</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>I recorded your 8:15 a.m. start, the exact 1.0MEX-0603 drawing discrepancy, and the added identity/value-verification workload—without inventing elapsed hours. Item 7 stays with you.</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>Evidence and workload record:</TextLine>
<TextLine>/home/omi/work_projects/dura/M3000/reviews/20260922-revX3_5/</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>Clean up conflicting component identities</TextLine>
<TextLine>These can result in the wrong assembly even with correct wiring:</TextLine>
<TextLine>R7/R8/R17/R18: 0603 footprints, but the specified MCR10EZHF1004 is an 0805 part.</TextLine>
<TextLine>U1: Name says N8R8, Value says N16R8.</TextLine>
<TextLine>L1: Name suggests 47 µH, while Value is 0.47 µH.</TextLine>
<TextLine>C17: reconcile its 10 nF value with the stored stock part number before purchasing/population.</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>Remaining risks—not established wiring failures</TextLine>
<TextLine>Supply envelope: C14 is only 16 V rated; the buck’s operating ceiling is 17 V. Establish the actual maximum supply/transient voltage and select protection/capacitor ratings accordingly. (2/3)</TextLine>
<TextLine>Output-driver dissipation: R21/R27/R30 carry continuous clamp current while ON. With an assumed 5.1 V clamp, each dissipates approximately 48 mW at 12 V, but 142 mW at 17 V. Check the actual resistor grade and temperature derating.</TextLine>
<TextLine>Timing capacitors: the specified C0603C105Z3VACTU parts are Y5V, +80/−20%, not stable timing capacitors. The output gate networks have a nominal 100 ms discharge time constant when the GPIO becomes high-impedance; that is not an instantaneous reset-to-OFF guarantee.</TextLine>
<TextLine>Customer demonstration configuration: the current local firmware still disables EV outputs and the external Recirc input. Its Recirc polarity/pull defaults also need reconciliation if the button asserts positive 12 V. This is separate from schematic correctness.</TextLine>
<TextLine></TextLine>
<TextLine>The spare output still matches the Recirc stage; I am not retracting that wiring check. The immediate priorities are the buck configuration/connections, PG bias, and missing U3 pad assignments.</TextLine>
</TextLines>
